WEBVTT

00:16.500 --> 00:18.460
Wake up. Wake up.

00:20.580 --> 00:22.630
It's morning. Get up, Nene.

00:29.720 --> 00:33.010
Clarin, did you waterproof your joints?

00:33.010 --> 00:34.720
They're fully sealed.

00:35.470 --> 00:37.310
Let me see your back.

00:42.520 --> 00:43.690
That tickles!

00:44.150 --> 00:45.780
Now it's your turn!

00:47.030 --> 00:48.570
"Ah!"

01:14.510 --> 01:17.970
Dark... Cramped... Scared...

01:17.970 --> 01:19.140
We're going out.

01:24.900 --> 01:30.360
This smooth sensation is undoubtedly the terra of a flat-chested maiden!

03:06.710 --> 03:08.460
Oh, Gercomas!

03:10.920 --> 03:12.090
Where are you going?

03:12.670 --> 03:14.630
Can we come with you?

03:17.390 --> 03:20.850
It's okay, I'll walk on my own. Thanks though.

03:24.730 --> 03:28.190
So, how many Gercomas are there anyway?

03:37.950 --> 03:39.700
Oh, Takumi!

03:40.120 --> 03:42.580
Gertsecommas are sketchy on the concept of individuality,

03:43.160 --> 03:46.750
so asking them vague questions like that is pointless.

03:46.750 --> 03:48.040
Behold!

03:49.000 --> 03:51.040
The Gertsecomma production plant!

03:54.300 --> 03:56.670
Say hello to my menacing machines!

03:56.670 --> 04:00.050
Each one is mass produced with precision and care.

04:04.600 --> 04:06.430
Ain't she a beaut?

04:08.770 --> 04:13.190
As of right now, 1,031 units have been produced.

04:13.770 --> 04:19.610
And Gertsecommas can easily change modes by transforming and specializing their machinery.

04:19.610 --> 04:21.700
It's my greatest work!

04:22.030 --> 04:24.700
But the fundamental layout and design is Uzal's.

04:26.200 --> 04:31.580
T-True, but all of Uzal's designs have this stupid round one-eyed thing going on.

04:32.340 --> 04:34.090
The eyeball makes it <i>adventurous</i>!

04:34.550 --> 04:37.220
After you saw the blueprints,

04:37.220 --> 04:39.340
your eyes lit up brightly.

04:39.340 --> 04:41.340
And then you immediately looked annoyed and said,

04:41.680 --> 04:46.180
"Well, if you <i>insist</i>, I <i>suppose</i> I could make this."

04:46.180 --> 04:49.140
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

04:50.390 --> 04:51.770
Takumi...

04:58.690 --> 05:00.450
Where are you going today?

05:00.950 --> 05:04.330
To the park. There's something I'd like to try.

05:04.330 --> 05:06.830
Watch out for them nasty bot-nappers.

05:07.160 --> 05:09.580
We will! See ya!

05:33.900 --> 05:35.400
This spot should do.

05:36.650 --> 05:39.190
Pandora Device, open!

05:40.070 --> 05:43.610
Decode skill, Elpis Series.

05:43.610 --> 05:45.200
Juggling!

05:51.000 --> 05:51.750
Wow.

05:51.750 --> 05:53.250
Look at that.

05:53.250 --> 05:54.500
She's got talent.

06:02.050 --> 06:03.800
Wow!

06:17.860 --> 06:19.360
Oh my.

06:23.110 --> 06:25.700
<i>I can even do things like this...</i>

06:26.620 --> 06:28.120
<i>Amazing.</i>

06:31.000 --> 06:32.750
<i>And everyone's enjoying themselves.</i>

06:42.510 --> 06:44.430
At water's edge, in everlasting summer,

06:44.430 --> 06:49.510
a scant chested maiden stares in melancholy as the breeze...

06:51.350 --> 06:52.930
Was there a system failure?

06:53.430 --> 06:57.810
The Pandora Device's functionality had appeared to be entertaining the crowd though.

06:58.520 --> 07:01.320
You're not wrong, but...

07:05.280 --> 07:10.240
Was this not a step towards the world peace Nene intends to bring about?

07:11.240 --> 07:14.000
I just don't think what I'm doing is right.

07:14.000 --> 07:17.000
I'm doing this with <i>your</i> power...

07:17.540 --> 07:19.380
Clarion belongs to Nene.

07:19.380 --> 07:20.750
Gay!

07:21.340 --> 07:24.880
It feels dishonest to use someone else's power for your own gain.

07:25.340 --> 07:28.930
Dishonest? In the sense of being unjust?

07:28.930 --> 07:29.640
Yeah.

07:30.300 --> 07:34.390
Can you accomplish world
peace all by yourself, Nene?

07:35.690 --> 07:37.650
Is using someone else's power unjust?

07:37.650 --> 07:40.440
Must a power be your own in order to be just?

07:40.440 --> 07:43.860
How much of this power can you call your own in the first place?

07:47.360 --> 07:49.660
Yeah, good point.

07:50.700 --> 07:53.160
It isn't all mine.

07:55.160 --> 07:59.170
It was given to me.

07:59.170 --> 08:02.420
Not by my parents, but by everyone.

08:02.710 --> 08:06.420
That makes me just a little dishonest.

08:12.760 --> 08:14.930
Oh, are you already done for the day?

08:14.930 --> 08:16.680
That's too bad.

08:16.680 --> 08:20.690
Maybe there'll be a second
performance soon, my little star?

08:21.020 --> 08:25.070
Oh, I'm sorry. It was just a bit of practice.

08:25.070 --> 08:27.570
How modest of you.

08:27.570 --> 08:31.570
You're more talented than the street performers
I've seen on the Avenue des Champs-Élysées in Paris.

08:33.200 --> 08:34.580
Thank you.

08:35.910 --> 08:38.330
But it's not really anything like talent.

08:38.330 --> 08:40.420
Of course it is, my dear.

08:40.420 --> 08:43.840
I had never expected that
rehabilitation would be so difficult.

08:45.670 --> 08:49.340
Just getting used to this hand was all I could do.

08:49.840 --> 08:53.220
Excuse me, I didn't mean to spring that on you so suddenly.

08:53.220 --> 08:55.100
My name is Anna.

08:55.510 --> 09:00.140
Oh, nice to meet you!
I'm Nene, and this is Clarin.

09:00.140 --> 09:01.100
Clarion.

09:01.520 --> 09:07.110
I was very much surprised to come across a young girl like you using her prosthetics so skillfully.

09:07.530 --> 09:11.030
In comparison, I've got a long way to go.

09:11.030 --> 09:13.370
Uh, I'm sorry.

09:13.370 --> 09:14.780
Don't be.

09:14.780 --> 09:16.790
You did my heart good, honestly,

09:16.790 --> 09:18.620
so I wanted to show my gratitude.

09:19.000 --> 09:20.620
Thank you.

09:22.830 --> 09:24.710
Um, I...

09:25.290 --> 09:26.460
Go on, take it.

09:26.750 --> 09:27.710
But...

09:27.710 --> 09:31.090
Children that work hard deserve a reward.

09:34.010 --> 09:34.680
Here.

09:35.850 --> 09:39.230
Thank you... ma'am.

09:39.640 --> 09:42.730
Bye-bye, Nene, Clarin.

09:50.440 --> 09:53.070
Children that work hard...

09:56.660 --> 09:58.870
'Nother one, damn it!

10:00.330 --> 10:02.370
Ma'am, you are consuming too much alcohol.

10:02.710 --> 10:04.000
Shaddup!

10:04.000 --> 10:05.750
Two drinks is plenty.

10:05.750 --> 10:08.420
Quit actin' like my mother, robutt!

10:08.420 --> 10:11.010
Friggin' robots, everywhere I go!

10:11.010 --> 10:14.590
I just lost another job 'cause of a damn robot.

10:15.090 --> 10:16.260
Enjoy.

10:16.260 --> 10:18.600
Whatever, just a part-time costume gig.

10:18.600 --> 10:23.230
And to top it all off, they want me goin' cyberized to keep workin' as a reporter!

10:24.600 --> 10:26.150
The world's gone to shit!

10:26.520 --> 10:27.650
Bill me.

10:28.110 --> 10:28.900
Yes, ma'am.

10:30.570 --> 10:32.190
Your balance is insufficient.

10:33.820 --> 10:35.410
Sign here, please.

10:36.070 --> 10:39.160
Your ID code too, please.

10:39.160 --> 10:40.660
Yeah, yeah...

10:40.660 --> 10:41.450
Huh?

10:42.120 --> 10:43.910
A network outage?

10:43.910 --> 10:49.920
Cenancle Island is currently experiencing
a large-scale network outage affecting all services.

10:50.250 --> 10:53.970
We apologize to all island residents for the inconvenience,

10:53.970 --> 10:56.430
and ask you to be patient as systems are restored.

10:56.760 --> 10:59.180
No use, bro. Won't budge!

11:00.430 --> 11:03.180
Whatever, makes our job easier.

11:05.440 --> 11:08.150
Oh? What's this?

11:08.150 --> 11:09.940
A network outage?

11:11.900 --> 11:12.860
What the...

11:13.400 --> 11:14.450
I'm...

11:36.510 --> 11:39.050
Even the 24/7 news feeds are down.

11:39.050 --> 11:40.760
I wonder if the trains have stopped.

11:41.430 --> 11:43.890
They have not given a time estimate yet either.

11:44.220 --> 11:46.890
Mine fifth leg hath whispered.

11:46.890 --> 11:48.850
It seems the network outage

11:48.850 --> 11:52.900
hath caused something to go awry
within Cenancle Island's core system.

11:53.190 --> 11:55.320
Why would such a thing happen?

11:55.320 --> 11:58.410
Thy world is built upon the
foundation of cause and effect.

11:58.860 --> 11:59.660
Cause and effect?

12:00.030 --> 12:01.080
Indeed.

12:01.080 --> 12:06.160
For instance, a certain city hath experienced a major
power outage, followed by a baby boom the next year!

12:07.160 --> 12:08.290
What's going on!?

12:08.290 --> 12:09.790
This's never happened before.

12:10.250 --> 12:13.210
Not an EMP, not a virus...

12:13.210 --> 12:14.800
Is Nene okay?

12:15.130 --> 12:19.800
Well, Uzal's puppet is with her, so I suppose she's fine.

12:21.640 --> 12:22.600
You two.

12:22.600 --> 12:23.310
Yes?

12:23.810 --> 12:25.310
Code Zero.

12:25.720 --> 12:27.310
Where is your administrator?

12:28.730 --> 12:30.100
No, um...

12:30.100 --> 12:34.070
Code Zero. Identify your model number and affiliation.

12:34.780 --> 12:36.940
Are your auditory elements functioning?

12:36.940 --> 12:39.240
Yes. Uh, I...

12:39.240 --> 12:42.240
You sure are a high-quality item, though.

12:42.240 --> 12:43.580
And with such natural responses.

12:46.870 --> 12:49.460
Um, I'm actually human.

12:49.790 --> 12:52.460
Human? But come on, you're...

12:52.750 --> 12:54.960
I'm a full-body cyborg.

12:56.920 --> 12:59.590
Oh, wow! Sorry about that!

13:00.180 --> 13:03.390
That was an extremely rude way to treat a young lady.

13:03.390 --> 13:06.600
Please don't worry, I'm used to it.

13:07.390 --> 13:09.100
<i>A full-body cyborg, huh?</i>

13:09.560 --> 13:11.480
<i>I've never seen one before,</i>

13:11.480 --> 13:14.110
<i>but this one seems a lot different than what I've heard about.</i>

13:15.020 --> 13:20.400
Thanks to these network outages,
robots in standby mode are being stolen en masse.

13:20.950 --> 13:24.240
It's not very safe, so you two
should go straight home.

13:24.530 --> 13:26.040
Thank you, sir.

13:26.040 --> 13:29.500
We <i>were</i> waiting for the train,
but I guess we'll walk home.

13:29.830 --> 13:34.590
I know it isn't much of an apology,
but let me escort you two somewhere safe.

13:34.590 --> 13:36.500
It's dangerous around here, too.

13:36.500 --> 13:38.130
Spoken like a wolf in sheep's cloth—

13:40.050 --> 13:42.180
Did you hear something just now?

13:42.180 --> 13:43.510
You imagined it.

13:44.300 --> 13:47.890
This network outage is a first for Cenancle.

13:47.890 --> 13:49.770
Jeez, you gotta wonder what's going on.

13:50.140 --> 13:54.100
I'm tired! Let's go home!

13:54.100 --> 13:57.150
I wish we could, honey,
but the buses aren't running.

13:58.280 --> 14:01.200
Sorry, mind if we make a quick detour?

14:01.200 --> 14:03.030
Sure, go ahead.

14:06.160 --> 14:08.410
Sorry, it's just in my nature.

14:08.410 --> 14:11.660
Not at all, I think this is very nice of you.

14:12.040 --> 14:14.170
Thank you so much.

14:14.170 --> 14:16.590
Bye-bye, miss!

14:20.050 --> 14:21.970
It's in my nature!

14:23.260 --> 14:23.930
I understand.

14:24.340 --> 14:25.970
We haven't introduced ourselves.

14:25.970 --> 14:29.010
I'm Robert. What's your name?

14:29.010 --> 14:32.310
I'm Nanakorobi Nene. This is Clarin.

14:32.310 --> 14:33.440
Clarion.

14:33.770 --> 14:37.400
Got it. Nice to meet you, Nene. Clarin.

14:37.400 --> 14:39.940
Nice to meet you too, Robert.

14:39.940 --> 14:41.240
<i>Clarion</i>.

14:42.530 --> 14:44.450
Hey, sorry again.

14:45.160 --> 14:49.160
I meant to get you home, but we
ended up going pretty far out of our way.

14:49.160 --> 14:52.040
It's no problem. I don't tire out.

14:52.040 --> 14:54.210
Help me!

14:54.790 --> 14:56.880
Best kinda loot—the kind that ain't movin'!

14:57.250 --> 15:01.460
Look bro, this pony's high-grade!
Thing's worth bank!

15:01.460 --> 15:04.880
Mii! Bring back my Mii!

15:04.880 --> 15:06.180
Are you all right!?

15:06.180 --> 15:08.720
Mii is family to me!

15:09.140 --> 15:11.600
Nene! You look after her!

15:12.770 --> 15:13.600
I'll go too!

15:17.270 --> 15:18.770
Clarin!?

15:20.190 --> 15:21.150
What was that?

15:24.610 --> 15:27.070
Huh!? Bro, where's my loot?

15:27.070 --> 15:29.620
What!? Mine's gone too!

15:29.620 --> 15:30.740
Bro, look!

15:31.330 --> 15:32.660
Wha—

15:32.660 --> 15:35.040
When did she get our goods!?

15:35.040 --> 15:36.420
Recovery complete.

15:37.880 --> 15:40.090
Look! It's a robot!

15:40.090 --> 15:42.670
Let's just take it with us.

15:43.760 --> 15:46.340
Here, robot robot! We're your humans.

15:46.340 --> 15:48.140
Don't disobey us.

15:48.140 --> 15:51.560
<i>Enemy threat confirmed.
Switching to combat mode.</i>

15:51.560 --> 15:53.020
Hold it!

15:53.600 --> 15:57.440
What you're doing isn't theft, it's kidnapping!

15:57.440 --> 16:01.020
Release the lady's family member immediately, and apologize!

16:01.940 --> 16:03.230
Huh?

16:05.190 --> 16:09.240
Save us the lecture and hand over the damn robot!

16:09.240 --> 16:10.620
Or you'll be sorry!

16:11.200 --> 16:15.330
She's not a robot! She's a wonderful lady!

16:16.910 --> 16:19.540
Bro, this dude's in our way.

16:19.540 --> 16:20.630
Well, what can you do?

16:21.000 --> 16:23.380
And too bad, since we hate violence!

16:24.760 --> 16:25.380
Mhm.

16:26.050 --> 16:27.880
I couldn't agree more.

16:27.880 --> 16:30.640
I was hoping we could settle this peacefully.

16:31.180 --> 16:34.350
Shit, how strong <i>is</i> this guy?

16:34.850 --> 16:36.560
Clarin!

16:36.560 --> 16:38.390
Robert!

16:40.230 --> 16:42.270
You got here at just the right time, girly!

16:42.270 --> 16:43.020
Nene!

16:50.030 --> 16:52.120
Everybody okay!?

16:52.120 --> 16:53.490
We're fine.

16:53.490 --> 16:55.660
Mii! Oh, thank goodness!

16:56.120 --> 16:57.750
Well, that's good to hear.

17:00.000 --> 17:03.960
I'm really sorry, but I've gotta make sure these guys get put away.

17:03.960 --> 17:06.920
It's no problem. The two of us can make it home.

17:07.260 --> 17:10.180
It's just not in my nature to let them get away with it.

17:10.180 --> 17:12.800
Sorry for getting you involved in this mess.

17:12.800 --> 17:17.180
Don't worry. I believe things like this get us one step closer to world peace.

17:20.140 --> 17:22.770
World peace, huh? That's great!

17:22.770 --> 17:25.070
I'll work hard to live up to your expectations.

17:25.440 --> 17:29.740
Take care getting home then, Nene. Clarin.

17:29.740 --> 17:31.070
<i>Clarion.</i>

17:32.740 --> 17:36.580
Hey Clarin, I think that was
another kind of world peace.

17:38.160 --> 17:39.290
Clarin?

17:40.250 --> 17:41.080
Anna!

17:41.540 --> 17:43.580
Are you all right, Anna!?

17:45.840 --> 17:47.340
Somebody!

17:47.340 --> 17:48.340
We need a doctor...

17:48.840 --> 17:50.470
An ambulance!

17:51.970 --> 17:53.220
What do we do?

17:55.350 --> 17:59.430
If there's something you want to do,
just use the Pandora Device.

18:01.180 --> 18:04.270
Is it just to have a power at your disposal and not use it?

18:04.270 --> 18:05.360
Clarin...

18:05.940 --> 18:07.480
Or is it dishonest?

18:09.480 --> 18:13.990
I want to help Anna! Please, Clarin!

18:20.830 --> 18:23.370
<i>Pandora Device, open!</i>

18:25.080 --> 18:27.880
<i>Decode skill, Elpis Series!</i>

18:28.500 --> 18:29.880
<i>Paramedic!</i>

18:32.340 --> 18:34.380
Anna, please stay strong!

18:36.510 --> 18:38.390
Accessing prosthetic limb!

18:38.390 --> 18:41.020
Acquiring vital signs. Reading clinical record.

18:41.560 --> 18:45.400
I know her full medical history, drug history,

18:45.400 --> 18:47.020
and how to deal with this!

18:47.480 --> 18:51.530
It's not my own power, but I want to help Anna!

18:52.150 --> 18:54.240
She doesn't just have a prosthetic limb,

18:54.240 --> 18:56.030
she has artificial organs too.

18:56.740 --> 18:59.910
She's not cyberized, so they're monitored by the city network.

18:59.910 --> 19:02.290
Then the outage must have caused problems...

19:04.920 --> 19:06.540
Pinpoint the symptoms!

19:11.090 --> 19:14.170
If I take over, I can keep it from getting worse!

19:14.670 --> 19:16.930
We've got to get her to a hospital right away.

19:16.930 --> 19:19.390
Nene, use them.

19:20.350 --> 19:23.810
Come out of hiding, Korobase's surveillance guards.

19:27.100 --> 19:30.320
They were concealed using thermo-optical camouflage.

19:31.070 --> 19:32.440
Gercomas!

19:34.860 --> 19:37.450
Just a bit longer, Anna!

19:43.870 --> 19:46.000
There's no need to worry now.

19:46.000 --> 19:47.960
It's a good thing you were treated quickly.

19:48.380 --> 19:50.960
Thank you, really. You saved me.

19:51.250 --> 19:53.760
No problem! I hope you get well soon.

19:53.760 --> 19:55.920
You were okay through all this, Nene?

19:56.260 --> 19:59.930
I'm a full-body cyborg, so I can handle a lot.

20:02.470 --> 20:07.270
Oh my, a full-body cyborg!
I've heard about them before, but to meet one...

20:08.310 --> 20:10.690
Good for you, Nene.

20:11.770 --> 20:13.820
Um, thank you?

20:14.190 --> 20:18.610
Please be advised, the network outage has been resolved.

20:18.610 --> 20:21.620
I repeat, the network outage has been...

20:26.540 --> 20:28.120
Good for you.

20:28.750 --> 20:31.630
That's the first time someone's praised me for it.

20:33.960 --> 20:37.170
<i>I did have help, though.</i>

20:39.720 --> 20:40.680
Hello?

20:40.680 --> 20:44.640
Nene, are you okay!? Nothing happened to you!?

20:44.640 --> 20:46.640
Don't worry, I'm fine.

20:52.110 --> 20:53.400
Pardon me, sir.

20:53.980 --> 20:56.230
Captain Robert Altman, reporting.

20:57.940 --> 21:01.870
What can I do for you,
Special Military Adviser Kurtz?

21:02.780 --> 21:07.370
You're late. It's 42 seconds
past the appointed time.

21:07.370 --> 21:13.420
I apologize, sir. The sudden network outage caused some chaos around the island.

21:13.880 --> 21:17.170
Time is the essence of life, Captain.

21:17.920 --> 21:20.970
Making light of it is barbaric.

21:22.050 --> 21:23.550
I'll remember that.

21:28.640 --> 21:32.650
I am requisitioning four of your
force's underwater duty robots.

21:32.650 --> 21:33.810
Have them prepared.

21:34.900 --> 21:37.650
Four <i>more</i> of them, sir?

21:38.150 --> 21:41.780
We presented you with six just last week.

21:41.780 --> 21:42.910
They were lost.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.280
What are you planning to—

21:45.660 --> 21:51.040
I don't need to explain myself to you.
Fulfill the request by noon tomorrow.

21:51.410 --> 21:54.880
Yes sir, Special Military Adviser.

21:54.880 --> 21:56.630
And regarding another matter:

21:56.630 --> 22:00.300
be sure to carry out the order
regarding Vulcan Harbor Park.

22:01.090 --> 22:02.430
Leave it to us, sir.

22:02.880 --> 22:05.680
It's all for the sake of world peace.

22:11.810 --> 22:14.690
<i>Nene, Clarin.</i>

22:14.690 --> 22:19.480
<i>Looks like peace on this island is going to take a strange turn.</i>

22:40.960 --> 22:43.970
Accessing the device named nature

22:43.970 --> 22:46.970
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:46.970 --> 22:47.510
read

22:47.510 --> 22:48.050
write

22:48.050 --> 22:48.720
enter

22:48.720 --> 22:49.350
close

22:49.350 --> 22:52.730
Exchanging loops causes inevitable encounters

22:52.680 --> 22:55.940
We need play doctor together!
I'd love to see you dressed up as one!

22:53.440 --> 23:04.030
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:55.940 --> 22:58.360
That's unnecessary. Nene can just use the Pandora Device and—

22:58.360 --> 23:00.360
Oh my god, I could be a nurse instead!

23:00.360 --> 23:02.190
And then I'd get to take care of you as a patient!

23:02.190 --> 23:03.950
Maybe I should drag Nene to the hospital.

23:04.030 --> 23:05.410
Saving data

23:05.410 --> 23:06.780
Strengthening predictions

23:06.780 --> 23:09.780
Even my latest updates

23:09.780 --> 23:15.080
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.080 --> 23:16.670
error error

23:16.670 --> 23:18.170
parameter

23:18.170 --> 23:21.500
Please help me understand

23:21.500 --> 23:23.670
where these emotions came from

23:23.670 --> 23:26.890
Find me at the end of this digital maze

23:26.890 --> 23:29.640
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.640 --> 23:31.640
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.640 --> 23:35.020
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.390 --> 23:38.020
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.360 --> 23:40.770
and head straight to you

23:40.770 --> 23:43.190
I won't come to understand love

23:43.190 --> 23:46.950
without having you here with me

23:54.080 --> 23:57.870
Robert, you're what they call a champion of justice!

23:58.830 --> 24:00.040
It's in my nature!

24:00.040 --> 24:01.250
I respect that!

24:01.250 --> 24:04.800
Nene, Korobase said you need to stop fixating on older men.
